{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.SpectralProjector","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.SpectralProjector","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SpectralProjector.eplus_add_eminus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SpectralProjector.eplus_add_eminus","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SpectralProjector.lean#L65-L69","doc":"**Completeness.** `e₊ + e₋ = 1` — the two spectral blocks resolve the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SpectralProjector.eplus_eminus_orthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SpectralProjector.eplus_eminus_orthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SpectralProjector.lean#L57-L63","doc":"**Orthogonality.** `e₊ · e₋ = 0` — the symmetric and antisymmetric blocks meet\nonly at `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SpectralProjector.eminus_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SpectralProjector.eminus_idem","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SpectralProjector.lean#L50-L55","doc":"**Antisymmetric projector is idempotent.** `e₋ = (q²−qσ)/(q²+1)`, `e₋² = e₋`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SpectralProjector.eplus_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SpectralProjector.eplus_idem","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SpectralProjector.lean#L43-L48","doc":"**Symmetric projector is idempotent.** `e₊ = (qσ+1)/(q²+1)`, `e₊² = e₊`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SpectralProjector.HeckeQuadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SpectralProjector.HeckeQuadratic","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SpectralProjector.lean#L39-L41","doc":"The Hecke quadratic in cleared polynomial form: `q·σ² = (q² − 1)·σ + q`\n(equivalent to `(σ − q)(σ + q⁻¹) = 0` for `q ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}